{"availability":"available","full":"amuta/kumi","name":"kumi","description":"Kumi is a declarative rules-and-calculation DSL for Ruby that staticaly analyzes and compiles your business logic.","category":"Business","language":"Ruby","stars":74,"forks":4,"created":"2025-06-27T01:47:04Z","updated":"2026-06-20T06:24:05Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":["brms","business-rules-engine","declarative-language","dependency-graph","dsl","framework","rails","ruby","ruby-gem","rules-engine"],"demo":"https://kumi-play-web.fly.dev/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:31.084Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:31.084Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:31.084Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T16:43:31.084Z","stars":74,"forks":4}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Kumi is a declarative DSL for calculation logic — tax rules, pricing, scoring, financial projections — that compiles to plain Ruby and JavaScript.","You declare the shape of your input data and the values you want computed. The compiler determines evaluation order, checks types, detects impossible conditions, and emits dependency-free code for each target.","No loops, no iteration plumbing: linetotals is computed per item because that's where the data lives, and fn(:sum, ...) collapses it back to a scalar. This works through arbitrarily nested arrays."],"features":["One source of truth, two targets. The same schema compiles to Ruby and JavaScript with identical semantics — write pricing logic once, run it in your backend and in the browser preview.","Broadcasting from data shape. Operations align over arrays automatically based on the declared input structure, including nested and ragged data.","Static checks at compile time. Type checking, dependency cycle detection, and unsatisfiable-constraint detection happen when the schema is defined, not in production.","Boring generated code. Output is deterministic, dependency-free, straight-line code with explicit loops. What you read is what runs."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/amuta/kumi/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"8b4c8f54e7fd1b0b847b80c634c5c08b34e780a97a2031162b532af835ff660f","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:31.179Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:31.179Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Kumi is a declarative DSL for calculation logic — tax rules, pricing, scoring, financial projections — that compiles to plain Ruby and JavaScript.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/amuta/kumi/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"8b4c8f54e7fd1b0b847b80c634c5c08b34e780a97a2031162b532af835ff660f","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/amuta/kumi/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:31.179Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-06-20T06:24:05Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/amuta/kumi/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:31.180Z","hash":"8b4c8f54e7fd1b0b847b80c634c5c08b34e780a97a2031162b532af835ff660f","originalBytes":7771,"storedBytes":7771,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["schema","docs","end","input","tax","items","kumi","let","ruby","price","item","logic","value","code","demo","open","over","schemas","array","call","doubled","export","imports","javascript","license","module","nested","per","runtime","sum","syntax","taxpolicy","total","what","acc18","amount","checks","compilation","compiler","data","decimal","extend","functions","fused","generated","i15","imported","language","line","live","payroll","pricing","rule","rules","scale","taxes","totals","across","aggregates","aot","arrays","arrays.","bands","broadcasting","calculation","cell","compile","compiles","composing","conway","dependency","dependency-free","detection","dsl","el14","employees","everything","examples","execute","financial","function","game","gem","golden","hash","identical","import","imports.md","install","integer","kernels","life","loop","loops","mit","mode","